00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:09.956
Problem.

5
00:00:11.206 --> 00:00:14.363
Implement an LFU cache with O(1) get and put.

6
00:00:14.643 --> 00:00:19.187
Evict the least frequently used key, and break ties by least recently used.

7
00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:23.883
Show why LFU resists a one-off scan that would flush an LRU cache.

8
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:26.108
Part 2.

9
00:00:26.388 --> 00:00:27.305
Key idea.

10
00:00:28.555 --> 00:00:36.022
Keep a map of frequency, then keys in LRU order (LinkedHashSet), each key's count, and the current minimum frequency.

11
00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:40.590
A hit moves the key from bucket f to f+1, which is O(1).

12
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.795
Eviction takes the oldest key in bucket minFreq, also O(1).

13
00:00:45.075 --> 00:00:47.486
A new key always resets minFreq to 1.

14
00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:50.180
Here is the diagram.

15
00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:54.947
Part 3.

16
00:00:55.227 --> 00:00:56.102
Solution.

